Package: mint-arm-vm
Version: 22.3.8
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Linux Mint ARM local build <mint-arm@localhost>
Recommends: spice-vdagent, qemu-guest-agent
Breaks: mint-arm-system (<< 22.3.6)
Replaces: mint-arm-system (<< 22.3.6)
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: Linux Mint ARM64 settings for virtual machines on Apple silicon
 What only virtual machines use in the unofficial arm64 build of Linux Mint 22.3 (the first
 start removes this package on a Raspberry Pi):
  - Firefox renders in software, because UTM's accelerated OpenGL (ANGLE, OpenGL 2.1)
    loses Firefox's text when Firefox draws with it
  - Apple Rosetta for x86-64 Linux programs when the VM runs under Apple's
    Virtualization framework with Rosetta sharing enabled
  - the QEMU guest agent and the SPICE agent's daemon keep running when Linux Mint's setup
    wizard hands over to the desktop, instead of stopping until the next start
  - on a system with an encrypted disk, the kernel's console is the VM's screen
    (console=tty1), not the serial port that the VM's firmware names, so that the
    passphrase prompt shows there; other systems start about 0.15 s sooner without it
